Package: empleR
Title: Tools for Analyzing Peru's National Employment Surveys (EPEN/EPE)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Valentina", "Linares Herrera", , "durgavalentinalinaresherrera@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Walter Omar", "Manky Bonilla",
           role = "ctb",
           comment = "Autor del indice de exposicion a IA incluido en el paquete")
    )
Description: Provides tools to download, read, and analyze microdata from Peru's
    national employment surveys: the Encuesta Permanente de Empleo Nacional
    (EPEN, 2022-present) and its predecessor the Encuesta Permanente de Empleo
    (EPE, until 2021), produced by Peru's Instituto Nacional de Estadistica e
    Informatica (INEI) and distributed through its public Microdata System
    <https://proyectos.inei.gob.pe/microdatos/>. Features include occupational
    code descriptions and documented crosswalks between CNO 2015 and CO-95,
    calculation
    of weighted labor market indicators with optional experimental survey-design
    inference, EPEN departmental-domain maps, and integration with an AI
    occupational exposure index.
